   "subject": "stacked graphs",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello,</div><div>.......... at this location:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/wiki/Align-two-plots-on-a-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/wiki/Align-two-plots-on-a-page&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368012010000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15eXPYGyx7o3GucQpu6sYQ\">https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/wiki/Align-two-plots-on-a-page</a></div><div><br></div><div>.... I found two routines which I tried to use</div><div>in Rstudio</div><div><br></div><div>.... both failed to run.  </div><div><br></div><div>The first resulted in this error msg: </div><div><br></div><div>Error in loadNamespace(name) : there is no package called ‘reshape2’</div><div><br></div><div>... the second got this error msg: </div><div><br></div><div>Error in loadNamespace(name) : there is no package called ‘digest’</div><div><br></div><div>I need to use something like these</div><div>techniques to create a stack of time histories</div><div>one above the other, with a common x-axis, no overlap,</div><div>all on one graph.  Ideally I would use several</div><div>features of ggplot to make the meaning clearer.   </div><div><br></div><div>Can you suggest a way I should proceed? </div><div><br></div><div>............. judson blake </div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bqJMf48XEAAJ",
   "from": "Crump, Ron",
   "author": "942ffec526d6a312",
   "date": "2016-04-25T07:48:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: stacked graphs",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Judson,\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt;Can you suggest a way I should proceed?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "I don&#39;t know how you install packages in Rstudio, but try installing\r<br>reshape2 and digest (see ?install.packages). If you still have a problem,\r<br>create a reproducible example (including data - see the link below), and\r<br>try asking again.\r<br>\r<br>Ron.\r<br>\r<br>&gt;Please provide a reproducible example:\r<br>&gt;<a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368012011000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ysSn3mdx1KLbWoeSUlnXk\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a>\r<br>&gt;&lt;<a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368012011000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ysSn3mdx1KLbWoeSUlnXk\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a>&gt;\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Nx0HfpMrEAAJ",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2016-04-25T13:55:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: stacked graphs",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><span style=\"color:rgb(6,26,153);font-family:Monaco\">install.packages(c(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;reshape2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,26,153);font-family:Monaco\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"> &quot;digest&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,26,153);font-family:Monaco\">))</span> will get you where you want to be.<div><br></div><div>Also, if you&#39;re wanting to put multiple plots in one window, check out the gridExtra package.  Example below.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\">library(<span style=\"color:#000000\">ggplot2</span>)</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\">library(<span style=\"color:#000000\">gridExtra</span>)</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">p1</span> &lt;- qplot(rnorm(<span style=\"color:#045218\">1e1</span>))</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">p2</span> &lt;- qplot(rnorm(<span style=\"color:#045218\">1e2</span>))</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">p3</span> &lt;- qplot(rnorm(<span style=\"color:#045218\">1e3</span>))</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">p4</span> &lt;- qplot(rnorm(<span style=\"color:#045218\">1e4</span>))</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,26,153)\">marrangeGrob(list(<span style=\"color:#000000\">p1</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">p2</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">p3</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">p4</span>), <span style=\"color:#000000\">nrow</span> = <span style=\"color:#045218\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">ncol</span> = <span style=\"color:#045218\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">top</span> = <span style=\"color:#b01600\">&quot;&quot;</span>)</div></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>david.</div><div><br><div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div>On Apr 25, 2016, at 2:48 AM, Crump, Ron &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">R.E....@warwick.ac.uk</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
